# clangd resolves the selected compilation database relative to this file:
# `build/` is the conventional default build directory for native/ — the
# qualified build dir on the macOS arm64 lane, and the same build the sweeps
# consume there. The qualified Linux aarch64 lane configures
# `native/build-linux-clang` instead; sanitizer lanes add `build/asan`,
# `build/rtsan`, `build/coverage`. Select whichever build you configured by
# passing `--compile-commands-dir=<build dir>` to clangd for the session —
# the database, the warning contract and .clang-tidy all flow through it.
#
# Compiler locations are deliberately NOT configured here: they differ per
# machine (Xcode toolchain `/usr/bin/c++`, Homebrew LLVM via `brew --prefix
# llvm`, distro `clang++-18`/`g++-13`) and the configured qualified compiler
# is already recorded in compile_commands.json itself. If your clangd needs
# help resolving system headers for a non-host toolchain, pass
# `--query-driver=<the compiler recorded in that build>` on the clangd
# command line — never bake an absolute developer-machine path into this
# shared configuration.
#
# Only -Werror is dropped so editor diagnostics don't double-gate what the
# sweeps already enforce.
CompileFlags:
  CompilationDatabase: build/
  Remove: [-Werror]
